 1 big thing — Exclusive: White House probes claims of missing Kennedy Center money 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photos: Charly Triballeau and Odd Andersen/AFP, and Erica Denhoff/Icon Sportswire via Getty Images President Trump has directed his White House counsel to examine explosive allegations dropped on him Friday in the Oval Office, Axios' Marc Caputo reports exclusively. 

 Former Trump attorney Alina Habba told the president that another one of his top advisers — former Kennedy Center leader Ric Grenell — failed to deposit a multimillion-dollar donation that her billionaire husband made to the center a year ago, according to four senior administration officials and three insiders briefed on the controversy.

 The total value of the contribution was nearly $6 million, White House sources said Habba told them. Grenell denied the accusations as "absurd" and a "lie."

 Grenell told Axios: "I've never asked for 1 cent to be sent somewhere else pretending it was for the Kennedy Center, and I've never received any payment from him at all. Make him give proof to what he is saying, not make these absurd allegations." Habba and her husband, Turhan Mildon, declined to comment through a spokesperson. Habba's attorneys plan to give the White House documentation — reviewed by Axios — to support her allegations.

 A White House official said: "The White House counsel has asked for documents and proof. None has come so far." A senior administration official cautioned that "these are only allegations. We don't know if they're true. This could be a misunderstanding."

 Said another: "POTUS doesn't want to deal with this. Of course, he's concerned. But if there is missing money, this is a big, big problem." The intrigue: Just a few months ago, Grenell was friends with Mildon and Habba. But he was notably absent from their $10 million wedding that was attended by Trump world officials, power brokers and luminaries last month.

 One Trump world insider with knowledge of the conflict said: "This is the ultimate MAGA blood feud." Keep reading . 

 
 
