 2. 📊 Poll: Texas is choosin&#x27; Dems 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios Texas Democrats are for the first time polling slightly ahead of Republicans in several big statewide races, Axios Austin's Nicole Cobler writes from a new University of Texas/Texas Politics Project poll . 

 By the numbers: Democratic U.S. Senate candidate James Talarico maintains a slim lead (50%-47%) over Republican Ken Paxton.

 In the governor's race, Democrat Gina Hinojosa leads Republican incumbent Greg Abbott 49% to 48%. For lieutenant governor, Democrat Vikki Goodwin leads Republican Lt. Gov. Dan Patrick 49% to 46%. Democrat Nathan Johnson leads Republican Mayes Middleton 48% to 47% in the attorney general's race. ✅ Reality check: All of these results are within the margin of error.

