 4. 🛫 1 for the road: The anti-LAX gets a glow-up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Travelers at Hollywood Burbank Airport's new terminal yesterday. Photo: Myung J. Chun / Los Angeles Times via Getty Images Hollywood Burbank Airport's new $1.3 billion terminal is open after nearly three years of work.

 The upgrades could solidify Burbank — BUR, in airport code-speak — as a viable, chiller alternative to the chaos that is nearby LAX. (Still, it only has 14 gates to LAX's 161.) Inside Hollywood Burbank Airport's new terminal. Photo: Myung J. Chun/Los Angeles Times via Getty Images The L.A. Times reports from yesterday's opening morning: "Instead of the snug, historic facility whose Spanish Colonial Revival style dated to 1930, travelers found themselves in a sleek terminal at Winona Avenue and Hollywood Way, distinguished by high ceilings, contemporary art, twinkling terrazzo floors, abundant charging stations and landscaping full of cactus and succulents, along with a few 'wet paint' signs."

